+Git root/common-directory values preserve identity whitespace; only the final protocol LF is removed. Canonicalization or UTF-8 failures refuse the observation instead of substituting another path. The external editor also checks that the live thread cwd belongs to the selected canonical worktree. Presentation escaping does not alter the editor argv.
+
+Ordinary Git probes retain at most 2MiB stdout and 64KiB stderr under the unchanged three-second deadline; status accepts at most 10,000 complete NUL-terminated entries. Overflow, invalid UTF-8, incomplete/unknown file records return an error, never a partial clean-tree observation. Review diffs keep their separate display-truncation policy. Immutable detailed change lists are shared on fanout and planning/Review clones; equal observations of the same worktree can share storage without merging timestamps or authority. This is a per-probe budget, not a global process-memory SLA.
